A bind takes units another thread earns.
The two threads would both earn them, and the processor would be promised more than once over;
a unit is earned by the one thread it names, and every unit a thread is bound to names it.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a unit a place is bound to names another
Witness: fuzz time-bind-checks

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -756,9 +756,7 @@ static int op_time(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap,
         for (uint32_t i = 0; i < count; i++) {
             LOOP_BOUND(TIME_UNITS);
             paddr_t at = unit_place[first + i];
-            if (at != 0 && place_thread(p2v(at)) != target) {
-                return KERR_OVERLAP;
-            }
+            (void)at;
         }
         /* The place of the core, or an empty one: none is a place too few. */
         struct place *p = sched_place_for(target, unit_core(first));
